---
import { Callout, CodeTabs, Icon, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const defaultCatalog = [
  { value: 'workspace', label: 'pnpm-workspace.yaml', language: 'yaml', code: `catalog:
  react: ^19.0.0
  react-dom: ^19.0.0` },
  { value: 'package', label: 'package.json', language: 'json', code: `{
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "catalog:",
    "react-dom": "catalog:"
  }
}` }
]

const namedCatalog = [
  { value: 'workspace', label: 'pnpm-workspace.yaml', language: 'yaml', code: `catalogs:
  react19:
    react: ^19.0.0
    react-dom: ^19.0.0` },
  { value: 'package', label: 'package.json', language: 'json', code: `{
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "catalog:react19",
    "react-dom": "catalog:react19"
  }
}` }
]
---

<Docs title="pnpm Workspaces" description="How Dep Beacon resolves pnpm workspace catalogs.">
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow"><span>04</span> / Shared dependency policy</p>
    <h1>One catalog.<br />A connected workspace.</h1>
    <p class="docs-intro">
      Keep version policy in one place. Dep Beacon resolves your pnpm catalogs before it analyzes each package manifest.
    </p>
    <dl class="docs-facts">
      <div><dt>Catalogs</dt><dd>Default + named</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Also supported</dt><dd>Overrides + package extensions</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="default-catalog">
    <h2 id="default-catalog">Start with a default catalog</h2>
    <p>
      Define your ranges in <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>, then reference them with <code>catalog:</code>
      in each <code>package.json</code>. Dep Beacon analyzes the resolved range, not the catalog reference itself.
    </p>
    <CodeTabs wrap={false} ariaLabel="Default catalog files" items={defaultCatalog} />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="named-catalogs">
    <h2 id="named-catalogs">Name a shared set of versions</h2>
    <p>
      Named catalogs let packages choose a specific version policy. Here, <code>catalog:react19</code>
      resolves the matching entry under <code>catalogs.react19</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeTabs wrap={false} ariaLabel="Named catalog files" items={namedCatalog} />
  </section>

  <Callout class="docs-note">
    <strong>Update the source of truth.</strong>
    <p>
      An update action on a catalog-backed dependency edits its owning entry in <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>.
      The package keeps its <code>catalog:</code> reference.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <section aria-labelledby="workspace-policy">
    <h2 id="workspace-policy">Bring the rest of your policy along</h2>
    <dl class="docs-reference">
      <div><dt><code>overrides</code></dt><dd>Central dependency overrides receive the same version and security
        signals as package manifests.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>packageExtensions</code></dt><dd>Additional dependency mappings participate in workspace
        analysis too.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>.yaml</code> or <code>.yml</code></dt><dd>Both supported workspace filenames work in VS Code
        and Zed.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <nav class="docs-next" aria-label="Related guide">
    <Link href="/docs/security">Understand security signals <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
  </nav>
</Docs>
